 The `cost` segment shows recorded session costs. For an active provider/model with scheduled pricing, it appends `↑` during peak hours or `↓` off-peak, refreshing at boundaries even while idle. The arrow reflects the current tariff, not past spending; flat-price models and explicit cost overrides have no arrow. See [usage costs and time-based pricing](models.md#usage-costs-and-time-based-pricing) for the UTC schedule and estimation semantics.
 
+`statusLine.segmentOptions.model.showAccount: true` (custom preset only) adds an account chip to the `model` segment: the OAuth account actually serving this session, plus one chip per advisor whose provider session resolved an account. A chip switches to the fallover glyph and warning color when that account is not the provider's pinned default (`providers.accountPriority` head or `providers.defaultAccount`). Chips only appear once a request has resolved a credential, and advisor chips are capped at two with a `+N` counter.
